v1.2.3 round-64 (2026.11.21): PR #57 CodeRabbit follow-up 2 — guard-script
  data-loss paths closed, meta sentinel V3-39 upgraded to
  implementation-line anchoring (baseline 44/27/40 unchanged).
  - Version: versionCode=10203, versionName="1.2.3" (unchanged).
  - verifier/runs/r62-negative-tests.sh (project script): the round-63
    hardening itself opened two DATA-LOSS paths (methodology §1.2, a
    defense mechanism's own side effects) — (1) the initial backup cp
    ran unchecked, so a full tmpfs / unreadable source would hand every
    later restore an empty/partial BAK to copy over ai-bridge.js,
    destroying the pre-run content; now cp + cmp -s byte-verified,
    aborting BEFORE any mutation (before the traps are armed, worktree
    untouched); (2) restore() deleted the backup unconditionally (a
    failed cp still rm'd the ONLY copy while 2>/dev/null swallowed the
    diagnosis) and the EXIT trap did not propagate the failure; now
    idempotent restore (absent BAK = success — the signal-then-EXIT
    double call cannot false-alarm), delete only after cp + cmp -s
    succeed, keep the backup + print its path + exit non-zero otherwise;
    the per-item restore in neg() gets the same check and aborts the
    mutation series on failure, leaving recovery to the EXIT trap.
  - verifier/v3/round54-pr56-triage.js (AGPL v3 harness): V3-39 upgraded
    from literal existence to IMPLEMENTATION-LINE existence — every
    property line-anchored (^ROOT=.*BASH_SOURCE/m, ^BAK=$(mktemp)/m,
    ^set -o pipefail/m, ^[^#\n]*FAILED=$((FAILED+1))/m,
    ^[^#\n]*[ "$FAILED" -gt 0 ]/m — a '#' comment line can never satisfy
    them) and the trap handlers must actually call restore (^trap\s+'
    [^']*\brestore\b[^']*'\s+EXIT|INT|TERM/m) — closing the live bypass
    where s.includes('mktemp') was satisfied by the header comment
    "exclusive mktemp backup" with the implementation line deleted, and
    the empty-handler bypass (trap '' EXIT) on the trap regexes. Same
    sentinel number, 25-assertion meta negative test suite (backup-cp
    failure, restore failure with backup kept, SIGINT 130 with no
    double-restore false alarm, empty handlers RED, implementation-
    deleted-comment-kept RED + old-check A/B bypass demo) in
    verifier/runs/round64-audit.md; all injections on /tmp fixture
    copies, the real worktree untouched.
  - License classification: all files unchanged.

v1.2.3 round-63 (2026.11.21): PR #57 CodeRabbit follow-up — negative-test
  script hardened, meta sentinel V3-39 added (baseline 44/27/40).
  - Version: versionCode=10203, versionName="1.2.3" (unchanged).
  - verifier/runs/r62-negative-tests.sh (project script): four review
    findings fixed — (1) the repo root self-resolves from the script
    location (BASH_SOURCE), removing the hardcoded sandbox path that
    fails the backup on other machines and would mutate/verify a foreign
    checkout where it exists; (2) exclusive mktemp backup with
    EXIT/INT/TERM traps armed before the first mutation (a mid-run
    SIGTERM can no longer leave an injected regression in the worktree;
    per-item restore kept); (3) failures accumulate — mutated=no (stale
    perl expression) or sentinel=NOT-RED now exit non-zero; (4) the
    final baseline propagates the verifiers' real exit statuses (set -o
    pipefail; a bare `node | tail` returned tail's 0), and v3 joins the
    final check because it also reads ai-bridge.js. Trajectory and the
    meta negative tests (broken-expression exit 1, SIGTERM recovery) in
    verifier/runs/round63-audit.md.
  - verifier/v3/round54-pr56-triage.js (AGPL v3 harness): NEW V3-39 —
    structural self-discipline guard over the negative-test script (no
    absolute paths, self-resolved root, trap recovery, exclusive backup,
    failure accumulation with a real exit gate, and this ledger pointing
    at the committed script path). Baseline 39 -> 40 (v1/v2 unchanged).
  - Round-62 ledger entry corrected in place (R61-a precedent): the
    negative-test script reference now points at the committed path (it
    previously named an uncommitted sandbox-tree location) and one
    filename typo is fixed (ai-bridge.js, not .java).
  - License classification: all files unchanged.

